# @USER@'s portal handover surface (issue #541), and the ONLY route on
# this vhost served without auth — trading a portal-signed token for a
# box session is what it is for, so demanding a box credential first
# would defeat it. Two endpoints live here: POST auth/handoff (the
# trade) and GET auth/verify (the forward_auth subrequest below).
# Neither discloses anything to a caller holding no token: verify
# answers 204/401 about a cookie the caller must already have, and
# handoff answers one message for every way a token can be wrong.
#
# The daemon 404s both unless this box was PROVISIONED for handover
# (portalUser + portalProject + an issuer + a key), so a box nobody
# wired to a portal serves no unauthenticated endpoint at all.
handle /@USER@/auth/* {
  reverse_proxy unix/@SETTINGS_SOCKET@
}
